  <running_head>De lingua Anglica vetere,</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">minus expertis sufficiant, quæ Caninius</l>
    <l n="2">&amp; Jul. Scaliger in hoc genere suppedi-</l>
    <l n="3">tant. Angli multa hodie exilius profe-</l>
    <l n="4">runt, quæ olim latius &amp; pleniùs. quod</l>
    <l n="5">discrimen etiam in hodiernis dialectis</l>
    <l n="6">obferves. Affixum privativum, quod</l>
    <l n="7">Anglis, leffe ; Belgis,loofe ; ut quod illi</l>
    <l n="8">goðloofe, Angli goðleffe, &amp;c. Ita illis</l>
    <l n="9">
      <bl>oogbe</bl>, <bl>ooie</bl>, <bl>oo</bl>, quod Anglis, <i>epes</i>,</l>
    <l n="10">
      <bl>hepie</bl>, <bl>eare</bl>, &amp;c. Ex Latino <i>lippus</i>,Bel-</l>
    <l n="11">gæ loope; ex pifcis,Galli <i>poiffon</i> effinxe-</l>
    <l n="12">runt. Sed &amp; in eodem ejusdem linguæ</l>
    <l n="13">dialectiq; verbo eadem varietas inter-</l>
    <l n="14">dum occurrit, ut foot,in fingulari ; plu-</l>
    <l n="15">rali, feet : ita tooth, teeth, &amp;c.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Eadem porrò diphthongorum quæ</l>
    <l n="17">vocalium ratio. aliæ aliis naturâ pro-</l>
    <l n="18">pinquiores, sed omnes permutabiles.</l>
    <l n="19">Sed &amp; vocales simplices in diphthon-</l>
    <l n="20">gas, &amp; diphthongi in vocales sæpè mi-</l>
    <l n="21">grant. Exempla apud Caninium,&amp; Sca-</l>
    <l n="22">ligerum quibufvis obvia. Multa quoq;</l>
    <l n="23">Robertus Stephanus, non ille celeber-</l>
    <l n="24">rimus, de melioribus literis meritiffi-</l>
    <l n="25">mus ; sed ejus opinor filius, Henrici</l>
    <l n="26">frater,in Grammaticâ suâ Gallicâ, La-</l>
    <l n="27">tinè Gallicéque excufâ : ubi Gallico-</l>
    <l n="28">rum verborum ex Latinis derivando-rum</l>
  </main_text>
